  <prompt>Wire the one-way `FeedbackService` (the `feedback` Cosmos container; thumbs up/down + ≤500-char comment; `SubmitAsync` ~:57 — nothing consumes it into memory today) into the governed memory write path so that a thumbs-down+comment OR an explicit "do this every time" standing directive persists a governed `Preference` memory item (from task 030) tied to that user, with correct `MemoryOrigin` / `ConfirmedByUser` semantics. Reuse the CRUD-safe capture facade discipline (`PublicContracts/IComposeMemoryCapture.cs` pattern). Keep it per-user only — NO global catalog mutation (ADR-039 catalog stays HITL). Keep `trustLevel` carried inert (ADR-042 #616).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. .NET 8 Minimal API + AI memory-governance expertise; comfortable with the ADR-042 memory model, the ADR-013 AI facade boundary (PublicContracts write-facades), and the Cosmos `feedback` / `memory-items` containers.</role>
  <goal>A thumbs-down+comment OR an explicit "do this every time" directive writes a governed `Preference` memory item (correct `MemoryOrigin` / `ConfirmedByUser`) tied to that user — closing the P3 learning loop that the one-way feedback sink leaves open today.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-08 — the second E3 step. `FeedbackService.cs` (`SubmitAsync` ~:57) writes thumbs up/down + a ≤500-char comment to the `feedback` Cosmos container, but it is a ONE-WAY SINK: nothing consumes it into memory today, so thumbs/feedback never improves behavior and the learning loop never closes. This task adds the pipeline: a governed trigger (an explicit standing directive such as "do this every time", and/or a thumbs-down+comment) writes a `Preference` memory item (the type added in task 030) via the memory write path, tied to that user, with `MemoryOrigin` (user vs ai-derived) and `ConfirmedByUser` set appropriately. The write reuses the CRUD-safe capture-facade discipline seen in `PublicContracts/IComposeMemoryCapture.cs`. It is strictly per-user: the ADR-039 global capability catalog stays HITL — no auto-mutation. ADR-042's deferred hard-governance stays deferred to #616 (`trustLevel` carried inert). Recall of the resulting preference item is already covered by task 030 (userFragment via `ToUserPromptFragmentAsync`).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Feedback/FeedbackService.cs (`feedback` Cosmos container; thumbs up/down + ≤500-char comment; SubmitAsync ~:57 — one-way sink today)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/MemoryWriteHandler.cs (the governed memory write path — reuse; Preference wired in task 030)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Memory/MemoryFactType.cs (`Preference` — added in task 030)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IComposeMemoryCapture.cs (the CRUD-safe write-facade pattern to mirror)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/MemoryItem.cs (v1 — MemoryScope/MemoryOrigin — bind consumers here)</file>
      <file>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (add/update unit tests — NFR-08)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039" scope="the pipeline's persistence target">Persist ONLY a per-user `Preference` memory item — MUST NOT mutate the global capability catalog (stays HITL); no auto-promotion of a user preference into shared/global state.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-042" scope="the memory write">Set `MemoryOrigin` (user vs ai-derived) and `ConfirmedByUser` per the actual trigger; preserve the deferred hard-governance (#616) — `trustLevel` carried INERT; do NOT implement untrusted-origin ban / trustLevel enforcement / memory-poisoning evals.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013" scope="the feedback→memory wiring">Write through the CRUD-safe capture-facade discipline (`IComposeMemoryCapture.cs` pattern); bind to `PublicContracts/MemoryItem.cs` v1; do NOT inject AI-internal types into CRUD code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="the pipeline">NEW wiring (nothing consumes feedback today) — reuse `FeedbackService` + the `MemoryWriteHandler` path; do NOT build a parallel feedback store or a second memory write path (§11).</constraint>
    <constraint source="BFF §10" scope="every BFF-touching change">Publish size ≤60 MB compressed (baseline ~49.63 MB incl. PDBs) — measure and report absolute + delta; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-08" scope="the pipeline">Add/update unit tests in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r4/spec.md</file>
