      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Define the trigger: an explicit standing directive ("do this every time") and/or a thumbs-down+comment surfaced through `FeedbackService.SubmitAsync` (~:57).</step>
    <step order="2">On the trigger, write a `Preference` memory item (task 030's type) via the governed memory write path, tied to that user (User scope), reusing the `IComposeMemoryCapture`-style CRUD-safe capture-facade discipline.</step>
    <step order="3">Set `MemoryOrigin` (user for an explicit directive; ai-derived where the pipeline infers it) and `ConfirmedByUser` appropriately per the trigger.</step>
    <step order="4">Keep it per-user only — assert NO global capability-catalog mutation (ADR-039 HITL); keep `trustLevel` inert (ADR-042 #616).</step>
    <step order="5">Add/extend unit tests in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (explicit directive persists a Preference item tied to the user; correct origin/confirmed semantics; no global mutation).</step>
    <step order="6">dotnet build + dotnet publish size check; record absolute size + delta; run the vulnerable-package scan.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If closing the loop appears to require mutating the global capability catalog or auto-promoting a user preference into shared/global state, STOP and escalate (ADR-039 HITL / owner Q4 out-of-scope operator queue) rather than widening beyond per-user memory.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>`FeedbackService` is a one-way sink (thumbs up/down + comment to the `feedback` container) — nothing consumes it into memory today.</existing>
    <extension>NO existing extension covers this — new wiring from feedback→memory; it reuses `FeedbackService` + the `MemoryWriteHandler` path (no new store).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Thumbs/feedback never improves behavior; the learning loop never closes — an explicit "do this every time" directive is discarded.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">the feedback→memory pipeline (Services/Ai/Feedback + governed memory write path)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ feedback→memory pipeline unit tests</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">An explicit standing directive ("do this every time") persists as a `Preference` memory item tied to the user.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The written item carries correct `MemoryOrigin` (user vs ai-derived) and `ConfirmedByUser` semantics for the trigger.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NO global capability-catalog mutation occurs — the write is strictly per-user (negative case, ADR-039 HITL).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The write uses the CRUD-safe capture-facade discipline and binds to `MemoryItem` v1; `trustLevel` carried inert (ADR-042 #616).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Unit tests added/updated in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ and pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size ≤60 MB reported (absolute + delta); no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Code-trace anchors: FeedbackService.SubmitAsync ~:57 (one-way sink); Preference fact type from task 030; IComposeMemoryCapture is the write-facade pattern to mirror. Depends on 030 (needs the `Preference` fact type). Task 032 consumes the persisted preference into a pre-turn tool hint. Run /conflict-check before the BFF PR.

COMPLETED 2026-08-17 (opus/high FULL). NOT committed/pushed (owner reviews governance-sensitive memory code). Files:
- NEW `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IPreferenceMemoryCapture.cs` — CRUD-safe capture facade (mirrors IComposeMemoryCapture): PreferenceCaptureInput + PreferenceMemoryCaptureOutcome/Status DTOs.
- NEW `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/PreferenceMemoryCapture.cs` — resolves AAD oid → canonical Dataverse systemuserid (ISystemUserIdentityResolver), builds a User-scope MemoryItem (Fact.Type=Preference), persists via SHARED IMemoryItemStore.UpsertAsync. TrustLevel=null inert; Tier-3 envelope; best-effort (never throws except honored cancel; unresolvable user → Skipped, NO write).
- EDIT `Services/Ai/Feedback/FeedbackService.cs` — injects the facade (optional, mirrors optional IAuditLogService precedent); after the feedback write, fires the trigger: standing-directive marker in comment (any rating) → origin=user + ConfirmedByUser=true; thumbs-down+comment w/o directive → origin=ai-derived + ConfirmedByUser=false; else no capture. Non-blocking (feedback id always returned even if capture throws).
- EDIT `Infrastructure/DI/AiPersistenceModule.cs` — registered IPreferenceMemoryCapture (Scoped).
- TESTS: NEW PreferenceMemoryCaptureTests (8) + extended FeedbackServiceTests (5 trigger cases). 20/20 targeted pass.
Governance: per-user ONLY (User scope, keyed by systemuserid — never oid, never Record/global); NO capability-catalog mutation (ADR-039 HITL preserved); trustLevel inert (ADR-042 #616 deferred). BFF build 0 errors; publish 43.67 MB compressed (≤60; no packages added); CVE clean. Step 9.5: code-review PASS (0 critical/0 blocking) + adr-check CLEAN (ADR-013/042/039/010, §10). Escalation trigger did NOT fire (loop closes wholly within per-user memory).</notes>
